WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV — time-as-an-index (30s) Narrator Hakim

1
00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:03.350
Sequential cryptography assumes you cannot look up the answer

2
00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:05.934
to a calculation before paying the steps to run it.

3
00:00:06.354 --> 00:00:14.413
Inside mathematical closed timelike curves, computational ciphers break at once—leaving only information-theoretic one-time pads.

4
00:00:14.833 --> 00:00:19.794
Thirty-one kernel-checked Lean 4 theorems and 65,536 SHA-256

5
00:00:19.794 --> 00:00:24.674
spectral runs confirm zero free shortcuts in known physics.

6
00:00:25.094 --> 00:00:28.945
Every real fast lookup is Hellman precomputation paid upfront—and

7
00:00:28.945 --> 00:00:31.966
a fresh random salt stops tables before they start.
